content.text:
Good.

Let's implement death fall and maybe fade screen. Small change.

In endGame:
```
if (!victory) { player.deathT=0; }
```
In animate result branch, before updateEffects:
```
if (player.dead) {
  player.deathT = (player.deathT||0) + rawDt;
  const p = Math.min(1, player.deathT / 0.55);
  player.group.rotation.z = p*p*1.45;
  player.group.position.y = -p*0.05;
}
```
But `player.group.rotation.z` starts 0. On retry, reset rotation.z=0 and position.y=0. In startGame set group.rotation.set(0, facing, 0). We already set rotation.y; add rotation.x=0; rotation.z=0. In returnToMenu too.

But note animateHero sets `rig.root.position.y` not group; so group position y reset? startGame sets player.group.position.copy(player.pos) => y=0. rotation z persists unless reset. Add.

Could cause renderer weirdness when dead rotating about world axes with camera; fine.

Maybe better fall backwards relative to facing; rotation.x = -1.45, not z, so falls backward from camera view. Rotating around x with root at feet tips the body backward/forward along local z; since group already rotated y, local x rotation tips backward relative to facing. Camera behind looking at back, so falls away from camera, natural. Use rotation.x += 1.45? Let's reason: hero facing away (rotation.y=π) means forward local -z? Actually group rotation.y=facing. With facing π, local +z maps to world -z. Rotating x positive tips top toward local +z? Rotation about x: y->z. A point at +y moves toward +z for positive rotation.x. With facing π, local +z = world -z (away from camera at +z? player at z9 camera z17, forward -z, so falling forward away from camera = world -z). So positive rotation.x tips forward away. Use rotation.x = 1.45. Camera behind sees hero fall away. Good. But group.rotation.y and x combined; fine. Add maybe `rig.aura.material.opacity` fade to 0.05.

Could also sink slightly? no.

Implement.

